{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09c236aab61d1e76634ebb0c80e05611f6879318c200c9827309986cd86890a1","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM completion-verification close gate","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/runaway_guard.py","src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","ToolCallLedger","read_file","_memo_toolsets","_runaway_guard_toolsets","record_executed","distinct_ratio","served_streak","completion_tool_policy.BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE","tests/unit/test_agent_call_memo_nudge.py","tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py"],"problem_keywords":["runaway-tool-loop","completion verifier","memo cache","tool loop guard","repeated file reads","memoization","layer composition"],"propositions":["The completion verifier loops on repeated memoized file reads, triggering RunawayToolLoopError despite prior runaway-guard fixes, blocking legitimate close operations.","The runaway guard sits outermost in the layer stack before the memo layer, so memo-served repeats are still counted as loop evidence even though they cost nothing and should not be punished.","The guard must observe and count only EXECUTED tool calls that bypass the memo cache, not model chatter served from the cache; a shared ToolCallLedger tracks executed vs observed calls with a served-streak backstop.","The composition fix reorders guard semantics via a two-arm guard: distinct-ratio computed over the EXECUTED stream only (arm 1), and a served-streak backstop for pure cache-served loops after a full window of zero-execution calls (arm 2)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787708230136339001,"uuid":"e84adbfb-302